var SEVERITY_LABELS = { BLOCKING: '🚨 BLOCKING', IMPORTANT: '⚠️ IMPORTANT' };
function severityLabel(severityClass) {
    return SEVERITY_LABELS[severityClass] || severityClass;
}
```

A human thread with no recognizable severity marker classifies `NONE` → `severityClassOf` → `SUGGESTION` (js/common/mergeBackstop.js:105-108), so the `open (human)` table shows a bare `SUGGESTION` string with no emoji — inconsistent with the labeled rows above it. Cosmetic only (the classification itself is correct: unmarked stays below the backstop threshold); adding `SUGGESTION: '💡 SUGGESTION'` and `NIT: '🪶 NIT'` to the label map would keep the table uniform.

